{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for the amendment-3 Room runtime exact head 8931f596920d3fe5c87bdc1321e8e303ff300b2b, all 15 submitted artifacts. The sealed carry/pin/advisory work is credited; two P2 job-delivery gaps remain.\n\n[P2] Expire or recover in-flight checker dispatches without suppressing the durable deadline retry. packages/room/src/jobs.ts issueJobs skips any core.running(job:id) before considering the expired sent row. RoomCore.kick keeps that key until service.handle resolves or rejects. If a service call stays pending beyond job.deadline, every jobs step skips it, next_ms remains the expired deadline, and nextAlarm remains in the past. Production alarmTime clamps this to now + 10 ms: repeated alarms neither retry the check nor move the debt forward. Independent actual Room DO/SQLite reproduction holds handle open with a controlled timer, advances the Room clock beyond the issued deadline, runs jobs twice, and observes exactly one dispatch, state sent/attempts 1, running true and past nextAlarm; it then releases/drains the call to keep the test bounded. Put a bounded dispatch/attempt lifetime under the durable scheduler, advance all unresolved work to a future due time, and fence late answers/finalizers from overwriting a newer attempt's state. Tests should cover a slow unanswered call through its deadline, retry/restart, a late refusal or answer after a successor started, expired token exclusion and no past-due hot loop.\n\n[P2] Issue jobs for preview integrations as required by R-EXEC-8. oweJobs is called only from landing readiness; its row/JobRow/issue logic requires a land operation. refreshPreviews can produce a clean integration while check obligations wait, but owes no job even for a whole-tree checker with a bound service and no snapshot dependency. Independent actual Room reproduction proposes a clean src change with its required whole-tree checker bound, drains preview/jobs steps before land, and observes clean preview, zero job rows and zero service calls. docs/protocol.md section 29.4 explicitly requires a preview's or landing operation's integration, so the README's landing-only choice is a scope deferral, not an underspecified contract choice. Add preview-owned job identity, current-integration/config/obligation fencing, base from the preview, and scoped snapshot recording when that dependency is available. Keep advisory work deliverable even if a landing finishes before its queued job starts; a nonblocking advisory must not silently vanish. Validate preview-before-land, preview refresh after main moves, invalidated generation/config and advisory dispatch.\n\nBoth probes pass as defect reproductions: /tmp/artroom-checker-RoomAm3-diagnostics/checker-amendment3-jobs.test.ts. Own initial preview assertion used the public word ready rather than the stored state clean; corrected before the completed run, not a candidate defect. Diagnostic removed from checkout; worktree clean.\n\nValidation: fresh npm ci --ignore-scripts (209 packages); full workspace typecheck; 67 Room Node + 295 Room workerd tests; unchanged integrated Git 143 Node and Log 127 Node + 122 workerd tests pass. Room Wrangler dry-run bundles 832.92 KiB with the actual Room/Registry/Publisher classes and Publisher container; this is not a live deploy and binds no checker service. Source/test/docs changes read in full against approved main 417a1618; git diff from that base contains exactly the 15 submitted paths, no unrelated changes. Base is an ancestor of current main ad19956b; the landed lane L check-carried decoder/verifier is retained exactly. Coverage /tmp/artroom-checker-RoomAm3-byte-credit.json. Candidate branch predates F carry UI; any landing must preserve the later approved main/UI work.\n\nArchitecture: carry outcomes and decisions are sealed transactionally, scoped to policy/integration and deduplicated; legacy unsealed rows do not count. Active reviewed configuration supplies the runner pin, admission refuses mismatch, and an unpinned checker can pass locally but never carry. Advisory flags come from reviewed configuration and are excluded from blocking readiness/reservation/land-rule inputs and relied-on evidence; compromised advisory evidence no longer stops reservation. Job authority remains the trusted service binding, with exact three-variable GitAuthEnv and read-only repository tokens. The scheduler must cover every promised lifecycle, including preview and unanswered calls.\n\nSecurity: no generic public job route is introduced, scoped jobs without SnapshotPort fail closed, and a mismatched published snapshot commit emits no job. Runner measurement/refusal remains the checker service's required work; a configuration pin alone does not establish that production measurement occurred. Whole-tree tokens are revoked on an answer or expire; future filtered repositories still need durable per-job revocation and repository retirement. Log decisions are replayable, but the known R-LOG-15 independent platform-proof gap/open point 34 remains required.\n\nSimplification: keep one durable logical-job state machine with fenced attempts and future due times, instead of an in-memory running flag that overrides durable recovery. Generalize the integration owner to preview or landing rather than a separate ad hoc preview queue. SnapshotPort is a useful fail-closed seam, but required item 4 (one repository per snapshot commit and durable cleanup) is not delivered: implementation request 23b96a18 must remain open until lane G/B helpers are safely integrated and all items pass. Real checker binding/deployment, whole-Room 128 MiB matrix 5a7290b9, full amendment runtime scope, preview jobs and other production integration requests remain required. Estimates affect sequencing only.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c76567cc1faf63f1444a92a8a16e9d709259b02d","binding":"assigned","head":"8931f596920d3fe5c87bdc1321e8e303ff300b2b","head_news_acknowledg